          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The yolk (the yellow part of an egg) of an ostrich egg is a single cell — the largest"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.335,
            0.16,
            0.634,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "known cell in the living world—measuring about 130 mm to 170 mm in diameter. The egg contains extra non-cellular"
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.226,
            0.633,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "material: a shell for protection and a white liquid that nourishes the cell during its continued development."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
