        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.288,
            0.556,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.3 What Are Microorganisms?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.325,
            0.744,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some living organisms are made up of just one or very few cells. They are so small that they can not be seen with the naked eye. These are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "microorganisms.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Some microorganisms, like bacteria and Amoeba, are made of just one cell (unicellular). Others, like some fungi and algae, have many cells (multicellular). They are found all around us — in water, soil, air, and even inside our body! But what do their cells look like? Are they like the plant and animal cells we just learnt about, or are they different? To observe the cells of a microorganism, again, we need to use a microscope which magnifies their size and makes them visible to us. Scientists have also created a low-cost and foldable paper microscope. Such foldable paper microscope may not provide the same level of details like high-powered laboratory microscopes. However, these make microscopic world accessible to many people."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.585,
            0.742,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us now take a closer look at the fascinating world of microbes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.622,
            0.656,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.4: Let us observe pond water/ stagnant water"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.68,
            0.743,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Take a container and collect pond or stagnant water in it with the help of your teacher or elder(s)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.719,
            0.743,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Use a dropper and place a drop of pond or stagnant water on a microscope slide. Put a coverslip and observe it under the microscope."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.775,
            0.743,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Observe the tiny organisms found in the pond or stagnant water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.83,
            0.693,
            0.854
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.5: Let us observe soil suspension"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.867,
            0.743,
            0.925
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z Take a beaker and collect some moist soil in it from the nearby field or garden. Do not touch the soil with your bare hands—use a spoon or gloves."
            }
          ]
        },
